# Techniques Source Summary

Techniques is presented as a universal mental model — a conceptual tool for navigating complex situations through pattern and relationship recognition. It draws on six influential sources: Robert B. Cialdini's Pre-Suasion, Timothy Ferriss's The 4-Hour Chef and Tools of Titans, Peter C. Brown et al.'s Make It Stick, Edward de Bono's Lateral Thinking, and Shane Parrish's Clear Thinking. The model functions as a meta-framework connecting learning techniques, influence strategies, creative thinking, and decision-making approaches.